12|Citrix Systems|2015-10-02|N|N|N||N|N|Retention Incentive Agreements for Henshall and Friedman. The text says 'as previously announced ... the search for a new Chief Executive Officer', which implies a prior CEO departure, but no departing person is named and no departure is reported in this filing. Coded N; round-1 rule 3 (a departure restated in a background sentence) could be argued to make this Y with restates_prior_disclosure = Y. [VERIFIED] NO. Citrix announced CEO succession on 2015-07-28; Mark Templeton was to remain president and CEO until a successor was appointed, and no successor had been appointed by the 2015-10-02 filing. No departure had occurred and none is reported in the filing. Code unchanged (N); flag REMOVED - the rules settle the case once the fact is known.
13|Citrix Systems|2016-04-01|Y|N|N|David R. Friedman, Chief of Staff, Office of the CEO (resigned effective immediately, 2016-03-31)|Y|N|Reported under Item 5.02(b). 'Chief of Staff, Office of the CEO' is not one of the enumerated covered titles and officer status is not stated in this text. Coded Y per round-1 rule 4. [VERIFIED] YES. Citrix's own 8-K of 2015-10-02 (sheet 12 of this draw) states the Incentive Agreements were with 'certain of the named executive officers listed in the Company's most recent proxy statement filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on April 17, 2015, which included ... David R. Friedman, Chief of Staff, Office of the CEO.' Corroborated by his prior role as General Counsel and SVP of Human Resources (2002-2015). Code unchanged (Y); flag REMOVED.
